(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111. Combines #109's deep free with #111's copy-in:
 `outer` holds independent copies of `inner_list` and `inner_map`, so
 `Free outer.` (which deep-frees everything OUTER's own slots hold) never
 touches the blocks `inner_list`/`inner_map` still name. Every original
 name stays fully readable afterward - the scenario #109's report flagged
 as an open hazard, now closed by construction rather than worked around.)

a list called inner_list is [1, 2, 3].
a map called inner_map is {"k": 9}.
a list called outer is [inner_list, inner_map].
Free outer.
print outer's length.
print inner_list.
print inner_map.
append 4 to inner_list.
On error print "should not be refused: inner_list was never freed".
print inner_list.
